{% doc %}
  Age bands — the size chips that sit at the top of an age collection.

  "Shop by Age → Newborn" answers half a question: a parent shopping for
  a four-month-old lands on 0–12 months and still has to read every card.
  This strip splits the shelf the way the menu already splits it, and
  filters it in place.

  ── How the filtering works ───────────────────────────────────────────
  Each chip is a tag URL — /collections/<handle>/<tag> — so Shopify
  itself narrows `collection.products` before the grid renders. No
  JavaScript, no second collection to keep in step with the first, and
  the browser's back button behaves. The active chip is read back from
  `collection.current_tags`, so a bookmarked or shared link opens with
  the same chip lit.

  A size nothing is made in yet is drawn but not linked. Shopify answers
  a tag URL that matches no product by silently redirecting to the whole
  collection, which would show a parent every size after they asked for
  one — so the chip says "not in this size yet" instead of lying. The
  test is `collection.all_tags`, which lists the tags actually carried by
  the products on this shelf, so the strip stays right by itself as stock
  changes.

  ── Where the chips come from ─────────────────────────────────────────
  Admin's navigation, never typed here. The section walks the chosen
  menu for the entry whose URL is this collection, and renders that
  entry's children in their menu order. Nothing to re-type when a band
  is added, and the header dropdown, the phone sheet and this strip can
  never drift apart — they read the same three levels.

  The section renders nothing at all off an age collection, so it is
  safe to leave in the collection template for every collection.
{% enddoc %}

{%- liquid
  assign menu = linklists[section.settings.menu]
  assign group = blank

  for link in menu.links
    for child in link.links
      if child.url == collection.url and child.links.size > 0
        assign group = child
        break
      endif
    endfor
    if group != blank
      break
    endif
  endfor
-%}

{%- if group != blank -%}
  {%- liquid
    # The tag a chip filters by is the last segment of its own URL, so
    # Admin owns the pairing of label to tag and this file never guesses.
    #
    # Which tag is live comes from the global `current_tags`: on this
    # theme `collection.current_tags` comes back empty on a tag URL, and
    # reading it alone lit "All ages" on a filtered shelf. The collection
    # form is kept as a fallback in case a future template populates it.
    assign active = ''
    for tag in current_tags
      assign active = tag
      break
    endfor
    if active == ''
      for tag in collection.current_tags
        assign active = tag
        break
      endfor
    endif
  -%}

  {%- comment -%}
    A thumbnail per size, uploaded in Admin. One block per band, keyed by
    the same tag the chip filters on, so a photograph is attached to a
    size rather than to a position — reorder the menu and the pictures
    follow. A band with no block, or a block with no photograph, falls
    back to the plain pill, so the run is never half-built.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- liquid
    assign shot_tags = ''
    for block in section.blocks
      assign shot_tags = shot_tags | append: ',' | append: block.settings.tag
    endfor
  -%}

  {%- comment -%}
    Horizon's own page grid, not sv-system's `.w`: the collection title
    and the filter row below both sit in the middle column of
    `.section--page-width` (40px | content | 40px), and a chip row that
    used the `.w` column started 43px to their right. Borrowing the
    theme's container is what keeps the three rows on one left edge at
    every width.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <section class="sv-bands section section--page-width" data-sv>
    <div class="sv-bands__col">
      <nav class="sv-bands__row" aria-label="{{ 'sections.collection.age_filter' | t | default: 'Filter by age' }}">
        {%- comment -%}
          Every chip is the same tile, photograph or not: a run of pills
          and tiles side by side read as two different controls and the
          row lost its line. "All ages" gets four dots rather than a
          face — it is the reset, not an age.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- liquid
          # "Everything 0–12 months" rather than "All ages": the range is
          # already written in the menu entry's own title — "Newborn
          # (0–12 months)" — so the reset chip names the span it clears
          # to, and Toddler or Kids say their own years without a second
          # setting to keep in step.
          assign all_label = section.settings.all_label | default: 'Everything'
          if group.title contains '('
            assign span = group.title | split: '(' | last | split: ')' | first
            assign all_label = all_label | append: ' ' | append: span
          endif
        -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          The reset chip shows the ages it clears to rather than a symbol:
          the sizes' own photographs, quartered into one circle. It is
          built from the same blocks, so it can never show a picture the
          run below does not. With no photographs set it falls back to
          four dots and the row still reads.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- liquid
          assign collage = 0
          for chip in group.links
            assign parts = chip.url | split: '/'
            assign t = parts.last
            for block in section.blocks
              if block.settings.tag == t and block.settings.image != blank
                assign collage = collage | plus: 1
                break
              endif
            endfor
            if collage >= 4
              break
            endif
          endfor
        -%}
        <a
          class="sv-bands__chip sv-bands__chip--all{% if active == '' %} is-on{% endif %}"
          href="{{ collection.url }}"
          {% if active == '' %}aria-current="true"{% endif %}
        >
          <span class="sv-bands__shot sv-bands__shot--all">
            {%- if collage > 0 -%}
              <span class="sv-bands__collage sv-bands__collage--{{ collage }}">
                {%- assign drawn = 0 -%}
                {%- for chip in group.links -%}
                  {%- if drawn >= 4 -%}{%- break -%}{%- endif -%}
                  {%- assign parts = chip.url | split: '/' -%}
                  {%- assign t = parts.last -%}
                  {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
                    {%- if block.settings.tag == t and block.settings.image != blank -%}
                      {{ block.settings.image | image_url: width: 220 | image_tag:
                        loading: 'lazy',
                        widths: '110,220',
                        sizes: '60px',
                        alt: '',
                        aria-hidden: 'true',
                        class: 'sv-bands__tile'
                      }}
                      {%- assign drawn = drawn | plus: 1 -%}
                      {%- break -%}
                    {%- endif -%}
                  {%- endfor -%}
                {%- endfor -%}
              </span>
            {%- else -%}
              <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" fill="currentColor">
                <circle cx="8" cy="8" r="2.6"/><circle cx="16" cy="8" r="2.6"/>
                <circle cx="8" cy="16" r="2.6"/><circle cx="16" cy="16" r="2.6"/>
              </svg>
            {%- endif -%}
          </span>
          <span class="sv-bands__label">{{ all_label }}</span>
        </a>

        {%- for chip in group.links -%}
          {%- liquid
            assign parts = chip.url | split: '/'
            assign tag = parts.last
            assign shot = blank
            if shot_tags contains tag
              for block in section.blocks
                if block.settings.tag == tag and block.settings.image != blank
                  assign shot = block.settings.image
                  break
                endif
              endfor
            endif
            assign made = false
            if collection.all_tags contains tag
              assign made = true
            endif
          -%}

          {%- capture inner -%}
            {%- if shot == blank -%}
              {%- liquid
                capture r
                  render 'sv-age-range', label: chip.title
                endcapture
                assign start_m = r | split: ',' | first | plus: 0
                assign stage = 'big'
                if start_m < 3
                  assign stage = 'newborn'
                elsif start_m < 6
                  assign stage = 'swaddle'
                elsif start_m < 9
                  assign stage = 'sit'
                elsif start_m < 12
                  assign stage = 'crawl'
                elsif start_m < 18
                  assign stage = 'toddle'
                elsif start_m < 24
                  assign stage = 'toddle2'
                elsif start_m < 36
                  assign stage = 'twos'
                elsif start_m < 48
                  assign stage = 'walk'
                elsif start_m < 72
                  assign stage = 'kid'
                endif
              -%}
              <span class="sv-bands__shot sv-bands__shot--drawn">
                {% render 'sv-baby', stage: stage, class: 'sv-bands__figure' %}
              </span>
            {%- else -%}
              <span class="sv-bands__shot">
                {{ shot | image_url: width: 220 | image_tag:
                  loading: 'lazy',
                  widths: '110,220',
                  sizes: '56px',
                  alt: '',
                  aria-hidden: 'true',
                  class: 'sv-bands__img'
                }}
              </span>
            {%- endif -%}
            <span class="sv-bands__label">{{ chip.title }}</span>
          {%- endcapture -%}

          {%- if made -%}
            <a
              class="sv-bands__chip{% if active == tag %} is-on{% endif %}"
              href="{{ chip.url }}"
              {% if active == tag %}aria-current="true"{% endif %}
            >{{ inner }}</a>
          {%- else -%}
            <span
              class="sv-bands__chip is-none"
              title="{{ section.settings.empty_text | escape }}"
            >{{ inner }}<span class="sv-bands__note">{{ section.settings.empty_text }}</span></span>
          {%- endif -%}
        {%- endfor -%}
      </nav>

    </div>
  </section>

  {%- if active != '' -%}
    {%- comment -%}
      Horizon builds its sort and facet forms against `collection.url`,
      which has no tag in it — so sorting a 6–9 m shelf, or ticking
      "In stock", threw the shopper back to every size without saying so.
      The forms are corrected to the path actually being viewed, on load
      and again on submit, because the facet block re-renders itself
      through the Section Rendering API and would otherwise come back
      with the untagged action. Progressive: with the script blocked the
      chips still work, exactly as before this file existed.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <script>
      (() => {
        const bare = {{ collection.url | json }};
        const tagged = {{ collection.url | append: '/' | append: active | json }};
        const fix = (root) => {
          (root.querySelectorAll ? root.querySelectorAll('form[action]') : []).forEach((f) => {
            const a = f.getAttribute('action');
            if (a === bare || a === bare + '/') f.setAttribute('action', tagged);
          });
        };
        fix(document);
        document.addEventListener('submit', (e) => { if (e.target instanceof HTMLFormElement) fix(e.target.parentNode || document); }, true);
        new MutationObserver((records) => {
          for (const r of records) {
            for (const n of r.addedNodes) if (n.nodeType === 1) fix(n);
          }
        }).observe(document.body, { childList: true, subtree: true });
      })();
    </script>
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endif -%}

{% stylesheet %}
  /* §02 of sv-system.css pads a bare <section> by 160px and paints it
     the cream ground; both are wrong for a filter row that belongs to
     the header above it. The host class on the section wrapper wins the
     cascade without touching the reset. */
  .sv-bands-host .sv-bands {
    padding-block: 0;
    background: transparent;
  }

  .sv-bands-host .sv-bands__col {
    padding-block-end: 8px;
  }

  .sv-bands__row {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 22px 18px;
    align-items: flex-start;
  }

  /* No card, no pill: the photograph is the control. Each tile is the
     same width so the labels sit on one baseline however long the run
     is, and the circle carries every state. */
  .sv-bands__chip {
    display: inline-flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 10px;
    inline-size: 128px;
    padding: 0;
    border: 0;
    background: none;
    color: var(--ink, #23201c);
    text-decoration: none;
    text-align: center;
    transition: color 0.18s ease;
  }

  .sv-bands__shot {
    display: block;
    inline-size: 120px;
    block-size: 120px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    overflow: hidden;
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--emerald, #17433a) 7%, transparent);
    transition: transform 0.18s ease, box-shadow 0.18s ease;
  }

  .sv-bands__img {
    inline-size: 100%;
    block-size: 100%;
    object-fit: cover;
    display: block;
  }

  .sv-bands__label {
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.02em;
    line-height: 1.2;
  }

  .sv-bands__chip:hover .sv-bands__shot {
    transform: translateY(-2px);
  }

  /* Selected: a ring set off the photograph by a hairline of the page's
     own ground, so it reads as a ring around the circle rather than a
     border drawn on its edge — which fought the collage's seams. */
  .sv-bands__chip.is-on .sv-bands__shot {
    box-shadow:
      0 0 0 3px var(--cream, #fbf7ef),
      0 0 0 5px var(--emerald, #17433a);
  }

  .sv-bands__chip.is-on .sv-bands__label {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--emerald, #17433a);
  }

  .sv-bands__chip:focus-visible {
    outline: none;
  }

  .sv-bands__chip:focus-visible .sv-bands__shot {
    outline: 2px solid var(--emerald, #17433a);
    outline-offset: 4px;
  }

  /* "All ages" is the reset, not an age: four dots on the brand ground
     rather than a face. */
  .sv-bands__shot--all,
  .sv-bands__shot--drawn {
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    color: var(--emerald, #17433a);
  }

  .sv-bands__chip--all {
    inline-size: 150px;
  }

  /* The quartered circle: two columns when there are enough pictures to
     fill them, one when there are not, so a half-built collage never
     shows a gap where a photograph should be. */
  /* The tiles must divide the circle, never overflow it: rows are stated
     as fractions of the circle's own height, because auto rows sized to
     the images made a two-photo collage twice as tall as its circle and
     only the first one showed. */
  .sv-bands__collage {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    grid-template-rows: 1fr 1fr;
    inline-size: 100%;
    block-size: 100%;
    gap: 1px;
  }

  .sv-bands__collage--1 {
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    grid-template-rows: 1fr;
  }

  /* Two: side by side, full height each. */
  .sv-bands__collage--2 {
    grid-template-rows: 1fr;
  }

  /* Three: one across the top, two beneath. */
  .sv-bands__collage--3 .sv-bands__tile:first-child {
    grid-column: span 2;
  }

  .sv-bands__tile {
    inline-size: 100%;
    block-size: 100%;
    object-fit: cover;
    display: block;
  }

  .sv-bands__shot--all svg {
    inline-size: 42px;
    block-size: 42px;
  }

  .sv-bands__figure {
    inline-size: 62px;
    block-size: 62px;
  }

  /* A photographed stage sits in the same circle as the line figures, so
     it is drawn a little larger and lifted to put its head on their eye
     line — a seated pose otherwise reads as sunk to the bottom of the
     circle beside a standing drawing. */
  img.sv-bands__figure {
    inline-size: 98px;
    block-size: 98px;
    object-fit: contain;
    transform: translateY(-4%);
  }

  /* A size nothing is made in yet: still shown, so the run of ages reads
     whole, but plainly not a destination. */
  .sv-bands__chip.is-none {
    cursor: default;
  }

  /* An empty size keeps its photograph in full colour — the owner reads
     a drained picture as a fault, not as a message — and says what it is
     in the label instead. */
  .sv-bands__chip.is-none .sv-bands__shot {
    opacity: 1;
  }

  /* Muted, not faint: against the cream ground the old 55% tint fell
     below comfortable reading. These hold the "not yet" reading while
     staying legible. */
  .sv-bands__chip.is-none .sv-bands__label {
    color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--ink, #1a1a1a) 78%, transparent);
  }

  .sv-bands__chip.is-none .sv-bands__note {
    display: block;
    font-size: 0.6875rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    text-transform: lowercase;
    color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--ink, #1a1a1a) 66%, transparent);
  }

  @media (max-width: 749px) {
    .sv-bands__row {
      gap: 16px 12px;
    }

    .sv-bands__chip {
      inline-size: 96px;
    }

    .sv-bands__chip--all {
      inline-size: 112px;
    }

    .sv-bands__shot {
      inline-size: 88px;
      block-size: 88px;
    }

    .sv-bands__label {
      font-size: 0.8125rem;
    }
  }
{% endstylesheet %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "SV Age bands",
  "tag": "section",
  "class": "sv-bands-host",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Shows the size chips from your navigation on age collections (Newborn, Toddler, Kids, Big Kids) and filters the grid by the chip's tag. Renders nothing on other collections."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "menu",
      "label": "Menu to read",
      "default": "main-menu",
      "info": "The menu whose third level holds the size chips."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "all_label",
      "label": "First chip label",
      "default": "Everything",
      "info": "The age range in the menu entry's title is added after it, e.g. Everything 0–12 months."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "empty_text",
      "label": "Empty-size note",
      "default": "not made in this size yet",
      "info": "Shown on hover and to screen readers for a size with no products."
    }
  ],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "shot",
      "name": "Size photograph",
      "settings": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "tag",
          "label": "Size tag",
          "info": "Exactly as it appears in the chip's link, e.g. age-0-3m or age-2-3y."
        },
        { "type": "image_picker", "id": "image", "label": "Photograph", "info": "Square crop; shown in a circle." }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "max_blocks": 12,
  "presets": [{ "name": "SV Age bands" }]
}
{% endschema %}
